    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe : used to enter cmd mode sometimes remains when backspacing out of cmd mode.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen nvim with ui2 enabled.\nType : and backspace.\nThe : remains.\n\nMinimal config i used for repro:\n```lua\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({})\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe colon disappears from pressing backspace\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.3\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim doesn't have ui2 and this doesn't happen on the stable ui\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS unstable (26.11.20260702.6517942)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nNixpkgs + mnw in a flake",
